<section class="sec problem">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-label label"><span class="n" data-flip>02</span><span>/ Problem</span></div>
      <h2 class="display">Agents can do the work. Nobody can trust them with the money.</h2>
      <p class="muted">On Solana, agents already trade, pay for data and hire other agents. The payment settles in seconds. What it bought, nobody checks.</p>
      <div class="split">
        <div><span class="label">Pay upfront</span><p>The agent can walk away with it.</p></div>
        <div><span class="label">Pay after</span><p>The agent has to trust you.</p></div>
      </div>
      <p class="closing">Today, agent commerce runs on <span class="strike" id="strike">hope</span>. MULE runs on rules.</p>
    </div>
  </section>